All 23 slices from the plan have been implemented on branch \`sandcastle/issue-366-luau-execution-polling-helpers\`.

### What was implemented

**New error classes:**
- \`PollAbortedError\` — returned when an \`AbortSignal\` fires during polling
- \`PollTimeoutError<T>\` — returned when the wall-clock budget is exhausted, carries \`lastObservedTask\` and \`timeoutMs\`
- Both re-exported from the package barrel alongside the other error classes

**Core polling loop** (\`resources/luau-execution/polling.ts\`):
- \`pollUntilDoneCore(deps, options)\` — injected fetch/now/sleep, configurable \`pollDelay\`/\`timeoutMs\`/\`signal\`
- Resolves on COMPLETE, FAILED, or CANCELLED terminal states
- Uses \`defaultRetryDelay\` (capped at 30,000ms) as the default backoff curve
- Pre-aborted signal short-circuits before any fetch
- Abort mid-sleep via \`Promise.race\`
- Abort after fetch but before next sleep (checks signal between iterations)

**Client wiring:**
- \`LuauExecutionClient.tasks.pollUntilDone(ref, options?)\` — polls with \`view=BASIC\`
- \`LuauExecutionClient.tasks.runUntilDone(params, options?)\` — submit + poll in one call
- \`PlacesClient.luauExecution.pollUntilDone(ref, options?)\` — smoke-tested smoke only
- \`PlacesClient.luauExecution.runUntilDone(params, options?)\` — smoke-tested
- Per-request \`apiKey\` override flows through to every polling iteration
- 429 bursts absorbed by the existing \`RateLimitQueue\` / \`executeWithRetry\` stack
- \`ResourceClient.sleep\` getter exposed for dependency injection

